From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:37:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000: Storage on every A8 board, Wi-Fi
 and Bluetooth on the iPhone 6

Only the iPod touch 6 (N102) enabled the ANS1 storage processor, and
only it described its BCM4345 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth module.

The ADT ans node of the iPhone 6 and 6 Plus (N61, N56) is the N102's;
the iPad mini 4 (J96, J97) has the iOS 15 form of it that the iPad Air 2
(J81) has, whose storage works with the same node. Enable ANS1, its
mailbox and the always-on power domain in t7000-common.dtsi.

Apple's device trees also give the N61 and N56 the N102's radio wiring:
Wi-Fi on PCIe port 1 (PERST# GPIO 77, device-wake GPIO 200) with REG_ON
on D2186 GPIO 10, Bluetooth on uart1 with power on D2186 GPIO 8 and
device-wake on GPIO 50. Move the module from the N102 board file to
t7000-bcm4345.dtsi, give the iPhone 6 its D2186 GPIO controller, and
let each board name its module (bacchus, tempranillo, barbera). The
iPhone 6's BCM4345B0 Bluetooth core uses the iPod touch 6 entry, whose
plain sequence it shares.

The N102 tree is unchanged. Untested on the other boards.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
